*  stlimit.sno -- a loop that never ends, stopped by &STLIMIT.
*  ERRORS: the loop has no way out, and &STLIMIT is what stops it.
*  Error 22. This is the one runaway in the set that the SNOBOL4
*  system handles itself: the machine never notices anything wrong,
*  and no instruction bound is involved. Compare noend.sno, which the
*  system cannot stop because it never finishes reading the deck.
*  Part of github.com/mdhender/sil. BSD 2-Clause; see LICENSE.
-LIST
        &STLIMIT = 20
        N = 0
LOOP    N = N + 1
        OUTPUT = N                              :(LOOP)
END
